    <title>Building and Deploying a Web App on Cloudflare Pages with Next.js, Hono.js, Drizzle and shadcn/ui</title>
    <link>https://gowinder.work/en/nextjs-honojs-shadcnui-drizzle-cloudflare-pages/</link>
    <pubDate>Mon, 26 Aug 2024 00:00:06 &#43;0800</pubDate>
    <author>Author</author>
    <guid>https://gowinder.work/en/nextjs-honojs-shadcnui-drizzle-cloudflare-pages/</guid>
    <description><![CDATA[<h1 id="building-and-deploying-a-web-app-on-cloudflare-pages-with-nextjs-honojs-drizzle-and-shadcnui">Building and Deploying a Web App on Cloudflare Pages with Next.js, Hono.js, Drizzle and shadcn/ui</h1>
<p>Lately I&rsquo;ve been taking advantage of Cloudflare&rsquo;s free offerings—both Workers and Pages. After tinkering with a few small projects and getting through the initial exploration phase, I&rsquo;d like to share the process of quickly building a <code>Web App</code> deployed on <code>Cloudflare Pages</code> using these open-source libraries.</p>
<p>If you don&rsquo;t want to read through the process, you can skip straight to the end. I&rsquo;ve shared the project address; just <code>fork</code> <a href="https://github.com/gowinder/cloudflare-pages-starter" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreffer ">my example project</a> and you can use it right away.</p>]]></description>
</item>
